# Migration guide

`externalFetch` has been replaced with `handleFetch`. Whereas `externalFetch` only ran when your `load` function contained a `fetch` call for an external URL, `handleFetch` runs for _all_ `fetch` calls in `load` that run on the server. Instead of receiving a `request` argument, it receives `{ event, request, fetch }`, where `event` is the underlying `RequestEvent` and `fetch` is SvelteKit's [internal `fetch` implementation](https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/load#input-methods-fetch).

```diff
-/** @type {import('@sveltejs/kit').ExternalFetch} */
-export function externalFetch(request) {
+/** @type {import('@sveltejs/kit').HandleFetch} */
+export function handleFetch({ event, request, fetch }) {
+  const internal = request.url.startsWith(event.url.origin + '/');
+  if (internal) return fetch(request);
  // handle external request
}
```

